The core generator is now in place and the paper’s gadgets verify exactly. A hard instance has 71 answer bits but expands to roughly 5,800 graph vertices; the checker avoids quadratic blow-up by proving that only vertex pairs at graph distance at most two need explicit comparison. I’m running the full 200,000-guess and adversary audit now.
