174:\begin{theorem}\label{theo:erric-exist-alt}
175-A graph $G$ has an ERR:IC if and only if it satisfies the following properties.
176-\begin{enumerate}[label=\roman*,noitemsep]
177-    \item $G$ is twin-free
178-    \item $G$ has $\delta(G) \ge 2$
179-    \item $G$ has no adjacent degree 2 vertices
180-    \item Every triangle $abc \in G$ has $|N[a] \triangle N[b]| \ge 3$
181-\end{enumerate}
182:\end{theorem}
183-\begin{proof}
184-First, we will show that these conditions are necessary for ERR:IC to exist.
