186-If $G$ has twin vertices $u,v \in V(G)$, then $u$ and $v$ cannot be distinguished, contradicting that ERR:IC exists.
187-If $\delta(G) < 2$ then $\exists u \in V(G)$ with $deg(u) \le 1$; thus, $u$ is not 3-dominated, a contradiction.
188-If there are two adjacent vertices $u,v \in V(G)$ with $deg(u) = deg(v) = 2$, then they will not be distinguished, a contradiction.
