Step 0 confirms the paper has one viable hard search problem: minimum ERR:IC is NP-complete by Theorem 3.1, while mere existence is easy by Theorem 2.3. The existing draft correctly chose the reduction but fails an important corpus constraint: its 383-bit detector choice was counted as “one atom” merely because it was packed into hexadecimal. I’m redesigning the Track B construction so the real witness has at most 256 Boolean atoms and difficulty grows through the constraint haystack, not hidden answer length.
